<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT - Cemex downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Cemex downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC James Capel said Wednesday it downgraded Mexico-based cement giant Cemex to hold from buy due to a recent share price appreciation.</p>
<p>-- &quot;At 47.5 pesos per share, Cemex has exceeded our year-end 1997 price target of 48.6 pesos per share in real terms,&quot; James Capel said in a statement.  </p>
<p>-- &quot;Cemex has outperformed the Bolsa by 6.6 percentage points in real terms and has appreciated 20.3 percent and 22.6 percent in local and dollar terms, respectively, since we initiated coverage on July 2,&quot; James Capel said.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Cemex shares no longer trade at a discount to its domestic peers, nor to its historical trading levels,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530.))</p>
